# Social Media Sentiment Analysis for Mental Health Awareness

End-to-end Python project: Twitter sentiment dataset → NLP analysis → mental health theme extraction → interactive dashboard → automated insights report.

## Dataset Summary (Inspected)

| Property | Training Set | Validation Set |
|---|---|---|
| **File** | `twitter_training.csv` | `twitter_validation.csv` |
| **Rows** | 74,682 | 1,000 |
| **Columns** | 4 (TweetID, Entity, Sentiment, TweetText) | 4 (same) |
| **No header row** | ✅ | ✅ |
| **Sentiment labels** | Positive (20,832), Negative (22,542), Neutral (18,318), Irrelevant (12,990) | Positive (277), Negative (266), Neutral (285), Irrelevant (172) |
| **Missing TweetText** | 686 rows | 0 |
| **Duplicate rows** | 2,700 | 0 |
| **Unique entities** | 32 (brands/games: Borderlands, Amazon, Google, Facebook, Microsoft, FIFA, etc.) | Same pool |
| **No timestamps** | ✅ (no date column) | ✅ |
| **No location data** | ✅ | ✅ |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The dataset contains tweets about **tech brands, video games, and companies** — not mental-health-specific content. The project will apply mental health keyword/theme analysis as an **overlay** on general sentiment data, flagging tweets that happen to mention mental health topics. This is a realistic NLP portfolio approach.

> [!NOTE]
> Since there are **no timestamps or location data**, Stages 13 (Time-based Analysis) and 14 (Geographical Analysis) from your outline will be **skipped** — we won't fabricate data.

