### Stage 3 — Data Cleaning

#### [NEW] [src/data_cleaning.py](file:///c:/Users/roshi/Downloads/REAL_WORLD_PROJECTS/Social%20Media%20Sentiment%20Analysis%20for%20Mental%20Health%20Awareness/src/data_cleaning.py)
Module that:
1. Loads raw CSV → adds column `original_tweet` (preserving raw text)
2. Removes rows where `TweetText` is NaN (686 rows)
3. Removes duplicate rows (2,700 rows)
4. Cleaning pipeline per tweet:
   - Remove URLs (`http`, `https`, `pic.twitter.com`, etc.)
   - Remove HTML entities (`&amp;`, `&lt;`, etc.)
   - Handle `@mentions` (remove the mention but keep for reference)
   - Handle `#hashtags` (strip the `#` symbol, keep the word)
   - Convert emojis to text descriptions (using `emoji` library or regex) for sentiment preservation
   - Normalize whitespace
   - Remove special characters but preserve apostrophes for contractions
   - Normalize repeated characters (e.g., "soooo" → "soo")
5. Creates `cleaned_text` column
6. Drops rows where `cleaned_text` is empty after cleaning
7. Saves to `data/processed/cleaned_tweets.csv`
8. Generates cleaning summary report to `outputs/reports/cleaning_summary.txt`

